    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/annevk/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/annevk/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/annevk/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/annevk/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/annevk/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "Since 50b3051, a mutation observer's node list only contains the nodes\npassed to observe(), but transient registered observers are added to\nnodes being removed. As a result, they were never removed: not when\nmutation observers are notified, not when observe() replaces the\noptions of the registered observer they originate from, and not by\ndisconnect(). In addition, since d34d52d, only mutation observers for\nwhich a record was queued are notified, so an observer that only got\ntransient registered observers, e.g., one observing attributes with\nsubtree when a child is removed, would not have them removed either.\n\nTrack the nodes that have transient registered observers in a new\ntransient node set and make the observer pending when a transient\nregistered observer is added for it. This means that removing a node\nfrom an observed subtree queues the mutation observer microtask right\naway, which can be earlier than before, e.g., for replaceChildren(),\nas that queues its record after inserting the new children.\n\nSince d34d52d, mutation observers are notified in the order they\nbecame pending, which differs from implementations. Rather than\nchanging that order in yet another way, notify mutation observers in\nthe order they were created, as implementations do.\n\nThis also:\n\n* Makes the original registered observer the source of a transient\n  registered observer created from another transient registered\n  observer, so that observe() removes those as well.\n* Makes observe() ignore transient registered observers when looking\n  for an existing registered observer. Otherwise observing a node that\n  was just removed from an observed subtree would modify its transient\n  registered observer, which is removed the next time mutation\n  observers are notified.\n* Avoids adding a transient registered observer to a node that already\n  has one with the same source.\n* Makes the move algorithm add transient registered observers as well,\n  as Chromium and Gecko do.\n* Makes queuing a mutation record only queue the mutation observer\n  microtask if an observer gets a record, as implementations do.\n* Makes disconnect() empty the node list.\n\nThis matches implementations, except that WebKit's moveBefore() does\nnot add transient registered observers yet.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63390\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * N/A\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63390\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/dom/1507.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 8, 2026, 9:50 AM UTC (ada81c8)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/dom/1507/b76da7a...ada81c8.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 8, 2026, 9:50 AM UTC (ada81c8)\">Diff</a>",
